  "tutWelcomeTitle": "Welcome",
  "tutWelcomeSummary": "Find your way around: the environment banner, the tabs and the tutorial controls.",
  "tutProductTitle": "Your first product",
  "tutProductSummary": "Hat: product manager. Create three components, a finished product and its bill of materials.",
  "tutWelcomeBannerTitle": "The strip at the top",
  "tutWelcomeBannerBody": "This strip always shows which environment you are in: its name and its kind. Amber means test, blue means tutorial and red means live data. The tutorial only runs in test and tutorial environments, so nothing you do here touches real data.",
  "tutWelcomeTabsTitle": "Tabs and sections",
  "tutWelcomeTabsBody": "The sections are on the left (or in the bottom bar on a phone). Opening a record, such as a product or a quotation, adds a tab to the workspace, so you can keep several records open and come back to them.",
  "tutWelcomeControlsTitle": "This card",
  "tutWelcomeControlsBody": "I am your narrator. Next moves on when a step is only an explanation. Steps that ask you to do something finish by themselves as soon as you have done it. Back and Skip step let you move around, and Pause hides me until you press Resume.",
  "tutWelcomeMenuTitle": "Where to find me",
  "tutWelcomeMenuBody": "Open the account menu to find the Tutorial entry. It opens the chapter map, where you can resume, replay or skip a chapter at any time.",
  "tutWelcomeProductsTitle": "Let's start",
  "tutWelcomeProductsBody": "Open the Products section. The next chapter starts there.",
  "tutProductOpenTitle": "Products",
  "tutProductOpenBody": "Today you are the product manager. Everything the company sells or builds is a product. Open the Products section.",
  "tutProductMotorTitle": "Component: Motor",
  "tutProductMotorBody": "Create the first component. Press New product, enter code TUT-MOTOR and name Motor, keep the type Purchased, and save.",
  "tutProductMotorHint": "The TUT- prefix marks tutorial data, so you can recognise it later.",
  "tutProductFrameTitle": "Component: Frame",
  "tutProductFrameBody": "Create a second component the same way: code TUT-FRAME, name Frame, type Purchased.",
  "tutProductControllerTitle": "Component: Controller",
  "tutProductControllerBody": "And a third one: code TUT-CTRL, name Controller, type Purchased.",
  "tutProductCartTitle": "The finished product",
  "tutProductCartBody": "Now the product you build from those parts. Create code TUT-CART, name Cart, and choose the type Manufactured: only manufactured products have a bill of materials.",
  "tutProductOpenCartTitle": "Open the cart",
  "tutProductOpenCartBody": "Open the new Cart product from the list to see its tabs.",
  "tutProductBomTabTitle": "Bill of materials",
  "tutProductBomTabBody": "Choose the Bill of materials tab. It lists the components needed to build one unit. A revision is a draft you edit, or the active one that production uses. Press Next when you are there.",
  "tutProductRevisionTitle": "A first revision",
  "tutProductRevisionBody": "Press New revision to start a draft.",
  "tutProductLinesTitle": "Add the components",
  "tutProductLinesBody": "Search each component and add it: Motor, Frame and Controller. Then press Save draft.",
  "tutProductLinesHint": "Type TUT in the search box to find the three components.",
  "tutProductActivateTitle": "Activate it",
  "tutProductActivateBody": "Press Activate. From now on production and quotations use this revision; later changes go through a new revision.",
  "tutProductDoneTitle": "Well done",
  "tutProductDoneBody": "You have a finished product with a bill of materials of three components. Later chapters build on it.",
